  "name": "ASMA (ANTI SMOOTH MUSCLE ANTIBODY) BY  IFA",
  "code": "2686",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Anti-smooth muscle antibodies (ASMA) are found at high titre in 70% patients with chronic active hepatitis.</p>\n<p><br>Low titre antibodies may be found in the sera of patients with viral infections, malignancies and in the normal population.</p>\n<p><br>ASMA show discrete staining of the muscularis layers of roden stomach and be seen on the inner muscular layer of blood vessels in&nbsp;rodents kidney.</p>\n<p>Other factors Including the clinical history and serological results must be taken into account for diagnosis. Auto Antibodies can be activated by a wide range of drugs including oral contraceptives and antibiotics.</p>",
